        "current_path": "semiotics/01-SAUSSURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:semiotics:saussure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "semiotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[saussure]",
        "section": "semiotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Saussure: Sign, Signifier, Signified",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "His central move: shift linguistics from the historical/comparative study of language change (19th-century philology) to the synchronic study of language as a system of differences."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-SAUSSURE.md#004",
      "path": [
        "01-SAUSSURE.md"
